WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:20.041
Mary led Dickon down the path to the place where the ivy grew thickly on the garden wall.

2
00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:26.038
Dickon felt as if he were being taken to look at a rare bird's nest and must move softly.

3
00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:31.382
When Mary stepped to the wall and lifted the hanging ivy, Dickon jumped back.

4
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.900
There was a door!

5
00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:38.306
Mary slowly opened it, and they walked into the garden.

6
00:00:38.307 --> 00:00:40.795
"Here is the secret garden.

7
00:00:40.796 --> 00:00:44.481
I'm the only one in the world who wants it to be alive."

8
00:00:44.482 --> 00:00:48.368
"This is a strange, pretty place," he whispered.

9
00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:52.495
"It's like we're in a dream."

10
00:00:52.496 --> 00:00:57.410
For two or three minutes, Dickon simply stood there looking at the garden.

11
00:00:57.411 --> 00:01:00.869
Then he began to walk around softly.

12
00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.039
He walked even more lightly than Mary had walked the first time she had entered the garden.

13
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.687
"I never thought I'd see this place," he said at last in a whisper.

14
00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:15.276
"Did you know about it?" asked Mary in her normal voice.

15
00:01:15.277 --> 00:01:17.692
Dickon made a sign to her.

16
00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:23.240
"We must talk quietly, or someone will hear us and wonder what's going on in here."

17
00:01:23.241 --> 00:01:30.098
"Oh, I forgot!" said Mary, feeling frightened and putting her hand quickly to her mouth.

18
00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:34.441
"Did you know about the garden?" she asked again quietly.

19
00:01:34.442 --> 00:01:40.919
Dickon nodded. "Martha told me. We used to imagine what it was like."

20
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.341
He stopped and gazed in wonder at the tangle of climbing roses in the trees.

21
00:01:46.342 --> 00:01:49.960
"Oh, the bird nests that will be here in springtime!

22
00:01:49.961 --> 00:01:54.041
It'll be the safest nesting place in England."

23
00:01:54.042 --> 00:02:00.090
Mary put her hand on his arm. "Will there be roses?" she whispered.

24
00:02:00.091 --> 00:02:03.427
"I thought perhaps they were all dead."

25
00:02:03.428 --> 00:02:10.148
"No. Not all of them. Look here." Dickon stepped over to a rose bush.

26
00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:14.813
He pulled a knife from his pocket and cut a lifeless-looking stem.

27
00:02:14.814 --> 00:02:18.465
"There's still green in that wood. Look at it."

28
00:02:18.466 --> 00:02:21.506
Mary was down on her knees in a moment.

29
00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:25.290
"When it looks a bit greenish and juicy like that, it's alive."

30
00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:27.510
He cut another stem.

31
00:02:27.511 --> 00:02:32.796
"But when the inside is dry and breaks easily like this, it's done for.

32
00:02:32.797 --> 00:02:34.377
There's a big root here.

33
00:02:34.378 --> 00:02:39.020
If it's cared for, there'll be a fountain of roses this summer."

34
00:02:39.021 --> 00:02:43.242
Mary smiled brightly. The roses were alive!

35
00:02:43.243 --> 00:02:48.707
The robin followed them as they went from bush to bush and from tree to tree.

36
00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:54.437
Dickon knew how to cut away the dry wood and could tell when a stem still had life in it.

37
00:02:54.438 --> 00:02:58.640
Within half an hour, Mary thought she could tell too.

38
00:02:58.641 --> 00:03:02.273
Mary's new gardening tools proved quite handy.

39
00:03:02.274 --> 00:03:07.899
Dickon showed her how to use the fork, while he dug about roots to let the air in.

40
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.994
They were busy working around a big rose bush, when he caught sight of something.

41
00:03:12.995 --> 00:03:19.153
"Who did that?" He pointed to one of Mary's own clearings around the pale green points.

42
00:03:19.154 --> 00:03:20.802
"I did."

43
00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:24.676
"Why, I thought you didn't know anything about gardening."

44
00:03:24.677 --> 00:03:30.175
"I don't. But they were so little, and they looked as if they had no room to breathe.

45
00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:34.809
So I made space for them. I don't even know what they are."

46
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:40.593
"You did exactly the right thing," said Dickon, kneeling next to the tiny plants.

47
00:03:40.594 --> 00:03:43.391
"A gardener couldn't have told you better.

48
00:03:43.392 --> 00:03:47.484
They're crocuses and snowdrops and daffodils."

49
00:03:47.485 --> 00:03:53.820
They agreed that there was a lot of work to be done and that Dickon would come to help her every day.

50
00:03:53.821 --> 00:03:59.249
"I wouldn't want to make the garden look too neat," he said cautiously.

51
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.950
"No, it wouldn't seem like a secret garden if it was too tidy."

52
00:04:03.951 --> 00:04:10.590
"This is a secret garden, sure enough, but I think someone else besides the robin has been working in here.

53
00:04:10.591 --> 00:04:14.555
Some pruning has been done more recently than ten years ago."

54
00:04:14.556 --> 00:04:19.108
"But how could anyone get in?" Mary was puzzled.

55
00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:23.621
Dickon shrugged his shoulders. "Let's plant your seeds."

56
00:04:23.622 --> 00:04:27.468
Mary held the seeds, while Dickon loosened the earth.

57
00:04:27.469 --> 00:04:32.576
"You're just as nice as Martha said you were," she said, smiling at him.

58
00:04:32.577 --> 00:04:39.969
"Now I like five people: you, Martha, your mother, Ben, and the robin."

59
00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:48.623
"Only five people!" Dickon laughed so hard he had to put his hand over his mouth to stifle the sound.

60
00:04:48.624 --> 00:04:52.181
"Do you like me?" Mary asked quietly.

61
00:04:52.182 --> 00:04:54.752
"I do. And so does the robin."

62
00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:58.995
He nodded toward the bird, who was perched on a tree nearby.

63
00:04:58.996 --> 00:05:02.626
"That's two for me then." She looked pleased.

64
00:05:02.627 --> 00:05:07.312
Just then the big clock in the courtyard struck Mary's lunch hour.

65
00:05:07.313 --> 00:05:11.476
"I have to go," she said sadly.

66
00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:15.040
She started toward the door but turned around.

67
00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:20.713
"Whatever happens, you would never tell anyone about the secret garden, would you?"

68
00:05:20.714 --> 00:05:26.652
"If you were a bird and showed me where your nest was, I'd never tell," Dickon promised.

69
00:05:26.653 --> 00:05:29.671
"Your secret is safe with me."

70
00:05:29.672 --> 00:05:34.396
And Mary was quite sure it was.
